meta {
  name: Configure Org OIDC
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orgs/{{orgSlug}}/oidc
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "oidc_issuer": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-id>/v2.0",
    "oidc_client_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "oidc_client_secret": "rotate-me-in-vault-once-sprint-3-lands"
  }
}

docs {
  Sets the federated IdP settings for one organisation. PlatformAdmin only.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; PlatformAdmin role enforced.
    2. org slug validated against ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,38}[a-z0-9]$ — 404 if invalid.
    3. oidc_issuer, oidc_client_id, and oidc_client_secret are all required.
    4. Client secret written to OIDCSecrets store (Vault > AES-256-GCM in DB > v0-inline).
    5. Organisation row updated with issuer, client_id, secret_ref.
    6. OIDC provider cache invalidated for this org.
    7. Write org.oidc_configured to audit_logs.

  Responses:
    200 OK                         — updated org object (secret not echoed back)
    401 unauthorized               — unauthenticated
    404 not_found                  — organisation not found
    422 validation_failed          — any required field missing
    503 secret_storage_unavailable — secret store write failed
}
